  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}+1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061x & =\\sqrt{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arctan}(\\sqrt{2}+1)=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{3\\pi }{8}+n\\pi .\n$$",
